WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.960
I’m often asked
what my opinion

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.520
about a diet
or disease is.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.840
Who cares what my or
anyone else’s opinion is.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.920
All we should care about
is what the science says.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.080
What does the best available
balance of evidence

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.000
Published in the peer-
reviewed medical literature

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.280
have to say right now?

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.720
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.280
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.480
Did you know that by age 50
about half of all men and women

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.080
will experience hair loss?

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.160
The majority of age-related
hair loss is genetic,

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.320
but even identical twins can have
dramatically different heads of hair

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.720
based on their diet and lifestyle.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.080
In our first story, we look at whether
biotin or zinc supplements

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.400
have any role in
preventing hair loss.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:59.280
“Studies show that by age 50,
approximately half of men and women

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.960
will experience hair loss.”

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.840
No, it’s not caused by
washing your hair too much,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.200
or brushing your hair too little,
two of the many myths out there.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.960
The majority of hair
loss with age is genetic

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:12.720
for both women and men,
in the case of this study.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.960
Based on twin studies, the
heritability of baldness in men

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.800
is 79 percent, meaning about
80 percent of the differences

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.480
in hair loss between men
is genetically determined.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.040
But that still leaves some wiggle room.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:31.440
Even if you have identical
twins, identical twin sisters

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.440
in this case with the same DNA,
one can have more hair loss

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.920
than the other thanks to Increased stress,

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.160
increased smoking, having more children,

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.360
or having a history of high
blood pressure or cancer.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.720
Smoking can contribute to
the development of both

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.200
male and female pattern baldness
because of the genotoxic compounds

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.040
in cigarettes may damage
the DNA in hair follicles

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.040
and cause microvascular poisoning
in the base of the follicle.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.120
Other toxic agents associated with
hair loss include mercury,

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.400
because it seems to concentrate about
250-fold in growing scalp hair.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.120
In fact, maybe the reason
Shakespeare started losing his hair

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.000
was due to mercury poisoning
from&nbsp;syphilis treatment.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.840
Thankfully doctors don’t&nbsp;
give people mercury anymore.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.120
These days, as the CDC points out,

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.400
mercury mainly enters the body
through seafood consumption.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.120
So, doctors should consider
screening for mercury toxicity

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.480
when they see hair loss, since there’s
something we can do about it.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.440
Instructing patients to reduce
fish intake and repeat blood tests

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.880
could offer relief of symptoms
and uncover dietary habits

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.080
that may be a source of heavy
metal-induced hair loss.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.600
Though admittedly, sometimes heavy
metal can lead to too much hair.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.480
What about nutrient deficiencies
as a cause of hair loss?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.920
After bariatric surgery, the most
frequent nutrient deficiency symptom

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.360
is hair loss, but that’s
because they’ve had their anatomy

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.400
rearranged to cause
malabsorption on purpose.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.720
In general, there is little
evidence to suggest that vitamin

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.040
and mineral supplementation
benefits people

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.920
unless they are actually deficient.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.960
For example, we’ve known
for centuries that scurvy,

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.640
severe vitamin C deficiency,
can cause hair loss,

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.880
but once you have
enough vitamin C such that

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.560
our gums aren’t bleeding,
there’s no data correlating

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.800
vitamin C levels and hair loss once you have

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.680
a certain baseline sufficiency of vitamin C.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.520
It’s also a myth that
supplements containing zinc

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.920
will increase hair growth,
unless you have zinc deficiency,

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.920
like if you’re an alcoholic or something.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.920
But if you have normal zinc levels
in your blood, taking more zinc

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:51.120
won’t help, and in fact can
have negative side effects.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.920
It’s the same thing with
taking iron supplements.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.440
The most common ingredient in
top-selling hair loss products

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.960
is vitamin B7, also known as biotin.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.320
Yes, biotin deﬁciency causes hair loss,

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.320
but there are no evidence-based data

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.760
that supplementing biotin
promotes hair growth.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.800
And severe biotin deﬁciency
in healthy individuals eating

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.520
a normal diet has never been reported,

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:23.200
but if you eat raw egg whites,
you can acquire a biotin deﬁciency

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.240
since there are these
compounds that attach to biotin

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.840
and prevent it from being absorbed.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.680
But other than rare deficiency syndromes,

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.600
it’s a myth that biotin
supplements increase hair growth.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.840
But hey, why not just have the
attitude "can’t hurt, might help?”

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.960
Because of the lack
of regulatory oversight

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:48.400
of the supplement industry
and, in the case of biotin,

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.080
interference with lab tests.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.600
Many dietary supplements
promoted for hair health

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.800
contain biotin levels up to 650 times

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.200
the recommended daily intake of biotin.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:03.440
And excess biotin in the
blood can play haywire on a bunch

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.560
of different blood tests,
including thyroid function,

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.800
other hormone tests
including pregnancy),

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.560
and the test they do to see
if you’ve had a heart attack,

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:15.600
so it could potentially
even be life or death

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:20.400
And in terms of poor regulation,
as I’ve done tons of videos about,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.920
there are all sorts of supplement
manufacturer shenanigans.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.960
For example, this outbreak
in which hundreds suffered

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.880
selenium toxicity because
they had an oopsie

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:36.240
and put 200 times the dose and
so it ended up causing hair loss.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.920
And the same thing can happen
with getting too much vitamin A.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.405
Next up, we look at
the pros and cons

00:05:43.405 --> 00:05:48.480
of the drugs finasteride
and minoxidil for hair loss.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.880
“Any consumer looking on the
Internet for a treatment

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.560
for hair loss is exposed to
a multitude of remedies.”

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.280
However, we only have good
evidence for efficacy for the

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:01.600
FDA-approved drugs,
finasteride, sold as Propecia,

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.080
and minoxidil, sold as Rogaine.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:08.880
It’s considered a myth that all
the patented hair-loss supplements

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.120
on the market will increase hair growth.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:15.600
And they may actually be more expensive,
with over-the-counter supplement

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:19.440
regimens costing up to more
than a thousand dollars a year,

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.360
whereas the drugs may only
be one to three hundred dollars.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.600
The drugs can help but
can cause side-effects.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:33.360
The Propecia can diminish libido
and cause sexual disfunction,

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.160
while the topical Minoxidil
can cause itching.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.440
To understand why there are
so many hormonal side-effects

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:44.400
for Propecia like impotence, testicular
pain, and breast enlargement,

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.840
you have to understand how the drug works.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.840
Androgens, male hormones like testosterone,

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.360
are the principal drivers of hair
growth in both men and women.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.800
We know this from studies
a half century ago

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:02.240
that show that castration
of men stopped hair loss.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:07.120
Why exactly were they being castrated?

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:11.360
Due to eugenics laws in the United States,

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.120
when mentally handicapped
persons were castrated

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.520
or had their tubes tied against their will.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.400
So-called retarded persons
were routinely sterilized

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.320
without their consent or knowledge and we,

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.040
the United States of America, was
the first country to introduce

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:34.320
eugenic laws, which were later
upheld by the US Supreme Court.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:38.720
In the 1930s, a vocal
proponent complained that

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.680
“The Germans are beating
us at our own game.”

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:47.920
Anyway, testosterone is the primary
androgen circulating in the blood

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:51.200
and can be converted to
dihydrotestosterone,

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:55.600
which is even more powerful by an
enzyme called 5-alpha reductase.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:59.280
That’s the enzyme that's
blocked by Propecia,

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.720
so it inhibits the souping
up of testosterone.

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.880
That’s why women are
not supposed to take it

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.440
since it could femininize male fetuses;

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.920
whereas for men it has
the sexual side effects

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:14.240
like erectile dysfunction, which
can affect men for years.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.040
It’s something the drug companies
had to disclose for the last decade:

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.840
“a difﬁculty in achieving an erection

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.960
that continues after
stopping the medication,”

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:27.360
side effects that may even be permanent.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:32.480
Up to 20 percent of subjects
reporting persistent sexual dysfunction

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.200
for six or more years
after stopping the drug,

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:40.080
suggesting the possibility
that it may never go away.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.000
What we think might be
happening is that the drug

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.880
may actually structurally
change the part of your brain

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.120
responsible for sexual function.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.040
And indeed, though blood
levels of hormones in users

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.600
with persistent effects appear normal.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.920
If you do a spinal tap and look at the
cerebrospinal fluid surrounding their brains,

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:00.880
neurosteroid levels do appear
to end up being altered.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:05.040
So, it's "recommended that
prescribers of ﬁnasteride,

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:09.520
as well as potential users, be
aware of the potential serious

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.240
long-term risks of a medication
used for a cosmetic purpose.”

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.640
To date, no new interventions
are used routinely

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:22.240
in the treatment of male or
female pattern baldness.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:25.040
Given the side-effects of
the current drug options,

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.440
there is a need for alternative treatments.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:33.200
So, what about foods? Things we
could eat to combat hair loss.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:38.000
That’s exactly what we’re
going to explore next.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:44.160
Androgenic or androgenetic
alopecia, also known as

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:48.080
male or female pattern hair loss,
is one of the most common

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.640
chronic problems seen by dermatologists.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:54.080
Wait, so it’s called male pattern hair loss

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.320
and female pattern hair loss?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.160
Yeah, in men they call it
male pattern hair loss,

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.000
and in women they call it
female pattern hair loss.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.320
Okay. Either way, it is characterized
by progressive hair loss,

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.560
predominantly of the central scalp.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:13.600
I’ve talked about
hair loss supplements.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.000
I’ve talked about hair loss drugs.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.080
What about foods for hair loss?

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:22.080
What role might diet play in
the treatment of hair loss?

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:27.360
Human experiments with fecal transplants
offer a clue to how powerful

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.840
our microbiome is, with reports
of improvements in hair loss

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:35.760
after a fecal slurry made from freshly
passed stools from a donor

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:41.360
was administered into another person’s
colon, and not just by a little.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:44.960
A totally bald guy starts
growing back hair a few months

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:47.440
after a fecal transplant and
a little over a year later,

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:49.280
check it out, completely regrown.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:54.320
The moral of the story is
not to drink brown smoothies,

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:57.280
but to keep your good gut bugs happy.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.960
Population studies have
found that male pattern baldness

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.960
is associated with poor sleeping habits

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:05.280
and the consumption of meat and junk food;

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:07.760
whereas protective associations were found

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:11.040
for the consumption of raw
vegetables, fresh herbs,

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.840
as well as the frequent
consumption of soymilk.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.840
Drinking soy beverages on a
weekly basis was associated

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.840
with 62 percent lower odds of
moderate to severe hair loss,

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:24.080
raising the possibility
that there may be

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:27.840
compounds in plants
that may be protective.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:31.360
Complementary and alternative
medicine treatments

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:34.320
“boast the ability to
’cure’ hair loss ‘safely’

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.520
with ‘less side effects’
than conventional medicine.

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:41.120
However, it is important...to look
beyond the overarching claims

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.560
and marketing to critically
review the literature.”

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:47.280
For example, many studies
have little relevance

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:50.240
because the evidence was
obtained on shaved rodents.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:55.920
Hey, let’s smear shaved
mice with bee venom.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:59.360
And even when they do clinical
studies on actual people,

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.400
sometime there’s no placebo
control; so, you have no idea

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.160
if the food had anything to do with it.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:08.560
But there has been a randomized
double-blind, placebo-controlled study

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:12.160
of compounds in hot peppers and soy,

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:15.280
showing significantly higher
promotion of hair growth.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:15.760
Here are some before-and-after
pictures of both men and women.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.800
Okay, but what kind of
doses were they using?

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:24.640
6 mg of capsaicin a day and
75 milligrams of isoflavones.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.000
Okay, what does that
translate out to in real food?

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.320
You can get 6 mg of capsaicin
in just a quarter

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:38.960
of a fresh jalapeno pepper a day.
That sounds pretty doable.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.000
And you can get 75 mg of isoflavones

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:46.000
eating ¾ of a cup of tempeh
or just straight soybeans.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.360
Soy nuts are even
more concentrated,

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:50.960
dry roasted soybeans,

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:54.160
but given the formation of
advanced glycation end-products

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.920
in high fat/high protein foods at
high temperatures, I’d suggest

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:02.080
avoiding routinely eating roasted or
toasted nuts, seeds, or soy.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:06.560
There’s also been a
randomized, double-blind,

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:09.360
placebo-controlled trial
of pumpkin seed oil.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.000
Where did they get that idea?

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:16.560
In 2009, a study out of South Korea
found that randomizing men

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:22.320
with BPH—enlarged prostate glands—
to just 320 mg of pumpkin seed oil

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:27.200
a day (that’s about 16th of a teaspoon,
so just a few drops a day)

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:30.240
improved urinary flow rates.

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:35.200
Urinary flow continued to kink off
and decline in the control group,

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.240
but those taking the equivalent
of just like eating two

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:41.680
single pumpkin seeds a day saw
a significant improvement.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:45.040
That would seem to be
an anti-androgen effect,

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.840
so maybe it would help with hair loss.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:50.560
It seems to work in mice
when used topically,

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:53.120
but what about in people
just eating pumpkin seeds.

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:54.400
It couldn’t hurt.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.147
Sadly, we often throw away
pumpkin seeds, squash seeds,

00:13:59.147 --> 00:14:00.880
or watermelon seeds, and
they actually have

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.760
a rich repertoire of nutrition.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.080
But you don’t know if they
actually work for hair loss,

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.840
until you put it to the test.

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:12.640
In a study, 76 men with male
pattern baldness received

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:16.160
400 mg of pumpkin seed oil
a day hidden in capsules,

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:21.280
or they took capsules instead of
the placebo for a few months.

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:24.160
Again, that’s only like eating
two pumpkin seeds a day,

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:26.960
maybe two and a half pumpkin seeds.

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:30.160
They measured scalp hair growth
with all sorts of objective

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:34.880
and subjective measures, and...
after 24 weeks of treatment,

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.120
self-rated improvement
and satisfaction scores

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:40.240
in the actual pumpkin seed
oil group was higher,

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.600
and they objectively had more
hair, a 40 percent increase

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:46.640
in hair counts compared to only
10 percent in the placebo group.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:51.840
In the pumpkin group, 95 percent
remained either unchanged or improved,

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.400
whereas in the control
group more than 90 percent

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.560
remained unchanged or worsened.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:00.480
Given such a pronounced
effect might we be worried

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:01.920
about sexual side-effects?

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:05.520
They looked before and after at
an index of erectile dysfunction

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:09.440
and found no evidence
of adverse effects.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.640
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.920
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:18.480
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.760
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:25.920
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:29.200
please go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:31.760
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:36.000
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite to each of these topics.

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:40.160
For a timely text on the
pathogens that cause pandemics,

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:43.040
order the e-book,
audiobook, or hard copy

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.920
of my last book,
“How to Survive a Pandemic”.

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:50.080
For recipes, check out
my second-to-last book,

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.320
my “How Not to Diet Cookbook”.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:55.520
It’s beautifully designed
with more than 100 recipes

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.600
for delicious and
nutritious meals.

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.320
And all the proceeds
I receive from the sales

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:02.720
of all my books goes to charity.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:06.800
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.960
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:13.200
on the latest in nutrition research
via bite-sized videos and articles.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.240
Everything on the
website is free.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.560
There’s no ads, no
corporate sponsorship.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:21.680
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:25.120
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:27.920
as a tribute to my grandmother,

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:35.840
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

